;s Mammals of the World</source><year>1999</year><edition>6th edn</edition><publisher-loc>Baltimore, London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>The Johns Hopkins University Press</publisher-name></element-citation></ref><ref id="b19"><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Potts</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Waugh</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bactrian camels and bactrian-dromedary hybrids</article-title><source>The Silk Road</source><year>2005</year><publisher-loc>Saratoga</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Silkroad Foundation</publisher-name><comment>Ed. by, Vol. 3, No. 1</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="b20"><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Przewalski</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><source>From Kulje across the Tian Shan to Lob Nur</source><year>1879</year><publisher-loc>Marston, Searle and Rovingron, London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Sampson Low</publisher-name></element-citation></ref><ref id="b21"><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reading</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name><name><surname>Enkhbileg</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Galbaatar</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Reading</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name><name><surname>Enkhbileg</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Galbaatar</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An introduction to the wild bactrian camel</article-title><source>Ecology and Conservation of Wild Bactrian Camels (<italic>Camelus bactrianus ferus</italic>)</source><year>2002</year><publisher-loc>Ulaanbaatar, Mongolia</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Mongolian Conservation Coalition &#x00026; Admon Printing</publisher-name><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>10</lpage><comment>Ed. by</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="b22"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ronquist</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Huelsenbeck</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><sc>mrbayes 3</sc>: Bayesian phylogenetic inference under mixed models</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><year>2003</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>1572</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12912839</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b23"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Savolainen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>YP</given-names></name><name><surname>Luo</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lundeberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Leitner</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic evidence for an East Asian origin of domestic dogs</article-title><source>Science</source><year>2002</year><volume>298</volume><fpage>1610</fpage><lpage>3</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12446907</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b24"><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schaller</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name></person-group><source>Wildlife of the Tibetan Steppe</source><year>1998</year><publisher-loc>Chicago, IL</publisher-loc><publisher-name>University of Chicago Press</publisher-name></element-citation></ref><ref id="b25"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stanley</surname><given-names>HF</given-names></name><name><surname>Kadwell</surname><give